  "description": "A quick overview what we are seeing, and looking for, in the markets",
  "body_html": "<p>The “BIG” announcement, wasn’t really that big after all. However, the fear of what the announcement could have been, was the major driving factor for driving stock prices down yesterday. We are seeing broad market recovery during pre-market hours. Will it hold? Good question, we will find out. I think it will…but let the price action confirm we are holding steady. </p><p>Constantly I see “Tim, should I buy the dip?!”. You can do whatever you want…but I do not.<strong> Buying the dip, and DCA is a BAD LONG TERM HABIT.</strong> You will get lucky a handful of times. We see it all the time. But when the market reverses into a more prolonged or extreme bear market, this almost always blows portfolios. No one has unlimited capital…so you can’t buy forever. </p><p>Below is kind of how I visually look for positions. I prefer a break out, with volume, at or near the local high (it may even be a 52-week high, or even an all time high!). Trend is friend here. When the market flips from just a “dip” into a full fledged bear market, I see this bad habit wreck thousands of investors and traders. All those gains over the past few months or years, wiped out. You will never catch the bottom or the perfect price, but you will ride a lot more trends with this habit. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OnWn!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F54e29141-c62e-4f88-9f53-f0b8f8a1ad57_1283x611.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!OnWn!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F54e29141-c62e-4f88-9f53-f0b8f8a1ad57_1283x611.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!